{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And I will establish My covenant, etc.</b> It should have been necessary to precede by saying ״וּבָאתָ אֶל הַתֵּבָה״ to the end, and afterward say ״וַהֲקִמוֹתִי אֶת בְּרִיתִי.״ And our Sages of blessed memory said (Genesis Rabbah 31:12): a covenant that the wicked of the generation would not kill him — end of quote. And according to this approach, it is necessary to precede ״וַהֲקִימוֹתִי״ etc. before ״וּבָאתָ.״" "<b>Further,</b> it appears that HaShem's intention was this: since He had decreed upon the people of his generation and said to him <b>all that is on the earth shall perish</b>, He was concerned that Noah might think that just as He had shown him in the earlier ones, so too would his fate and the fate of his seed overtake them to be blotted out in another generation — and this would be a rescue with no lasting rescue. Therefore He immediately hinted to him what He would do in the end, that He would establish a covenant with him never again to bring a flood and never again to cut off all flesh. And this is the measure of the verse: <b>all that is on the earth shall perish, and I will establish My covenant with you</b> — that such a thing will not befall you — and to escape the prevalent evil, ״וּבָאתָ אֶל הַתֵּבָה״ etc." "<b>Further,</b> it may intend to say that He established with him a covenant that He would not forget him in the ark, so that he would not be lost on his own. And this is what stood him in good stead, as it is said (Genesis 8:1): ״וַיִּזְכֹּר אֱלֹהִים אֶת נֹחַ״ etc. ״וַיַּעֲבֵר״ etc. ״רוּחַ עַל הָאָרֶץ״ etc., and afterward He commanded him to enter the ark, in fulfillment of this covenant. And although the covenant is not mentioned there, He relied on what was mentioned here. And it is possible that He alluded to this by saying ״וַיִּזְכֹּר אֱלֹהִים,״ for this Name is invoked over justice, and in judgment He remembered the covenant. And our Sages of blessed memory expounded (Genesis Rabbah chapter 33) that He transformed justice into mercy on account of his righteousness, and this is the way of derash."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:39:59.186059603Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}